dia experience, the child's own or the class-shared one, marked the same. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: a unified narrated piece (grade 2). Tools: the screening-plan card, the source card, the sound-cue card, Curio Class's own. Free path: found objects for sound, scrap paper books. Once-a-week path: 4 sessions | Last in grade 1 because the tale joins the year's order, pattern and roles and ends the year after the year-end check (week 27); this unit's showing is its own assessment | Candidate: the sound-cue step tried with a quiet version (a visual cue card) for a child who is sensitive to noise | Kahlo: the unit tells her art, her garden and her animals as the book does; her illness and injury are named only as the book names them, and the sensitivity agent reads Morales's own published words on the book first. No child dresses as Kahlo or imitates her look (APPROACH: never by costume). Sound: shakers at low volume; hearing protection offered. Family yes for showing outside class. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
