| Judging media | ma-k-judge (unit 3, days 43 to 52) | ma-g1-judge (unit 7): meaning, the part that works best, a change for viewers | ma-g2-judge (unit 11) retrieves ma-g1-judge (unit 7, days 107 to 116): purpose and setting, how well it works | Noticing and liking, then meaning and viewers, then purpose, setting and improvement |
| Joining and showing | ma-k-present (unit 4, days 55 to 64) | ma-g1-present (unit 8): a picture-book tale, one task in the showing | ma-g2-present (unit 12) retrieves ma-g1-present (unit 8, days 119 to 128): a narrated piece, the showing conditions named | Two art forms joined with help, then subject, art and sound in a tale, then one unified narrated piece |
| Sources and experience | ma-k-sources (unit 4, days 55 to 64) | ma-g1-sources (unit 8): an interest and a named example as sources | ma-g2-sources (unit 12) retrieves ma-g1-sources (unit 8, days 119 to 128): what you know, like and have read, credited | Own experience, then an example named, then reading and open sources credited |

### Handed on to Media Arts, grades 3 to 5

| This course hands on | Unit here | Row that picks it up (grade 3) | What grade 3 does with it |
|---|---|---|---|
| ma-g2-read | 9 | ma-g3-read | Takes apart how a piece's parts build its message and how a technique or style steers the audience |
| ma-g2-society | 9 | ma-g3-society | Media as a shaper of values and online behavior, tools and spaces examined for safe, fair use |
| ma-g2-ideas | 10 | ma-g3-ideas | Several ideas with different tools, tested with classmates before making |
| ma-g2-craft | 10 | ma-g3-craft | Group roles such as composing or tool handling; tools used in their standard ways |
| ma-g2-make | 11 | ma-g3-make | Content put in a purposeful order; a stressed element analyzed |
| ma-g2-judge | 11 | ma-g3-judge | The first named criteria, with a judgment given with them |
| ma-g2-present | 12 | ma-g3-present | A role and steps for sharing a piece, and a suggested improvement |
| ma-g2-sources | 12 | ma-g3-sources | An outside source and a source log; how popular media shapes meaning |

Each hand-on above is answered at both ends in data/progressions/arts.csv (the grade 3 rows' `assumes` cells); this
table follows those rows.

## Models carried

| Model | Where it comes from | Introduced or first used here | Used again here |
|---|---|---|---|
| look-describe-interpret | New in kindergarten (ma-k-read, model_out) | Unit 1: notice the parts of a piece and tell what it seems to say | Unit 5 (contents and messages, two pieces compared, ma-g1-read), unit 9 (how pieces shape experiences, ma-g2-read); every unit's talk about a work uses it as review |
| media-ethics-check | New in kindergarten (ma-k-society, model_out) | Unit 1: the media rules card in pictures (two hands, set it down, ask first, no faces, wait your turn) | Unit 5 (fair play and the class rules written together, ma-g1-society), unit 9 (rules for a group project, with credit, ma-g2-society); every tool day as review |
| storyboard | New in kindergarten (ma-k-ideas, model_out) | Unit 2: the three-box card (first, next, last) | Unit 6 (sketches in order and a mockup, ma-g1-ideas), unit 10 (many ideas, one chosen, ma-g2-ideas); units 3, 7 and 11 make from it as review |
| production-roles | New in kindergarten (ma-k-craft, model_out) | Unit 2: a part in the partner shadow piece (puppet mover, light holder, sound maker) | Unit 6 (named roles, ma-g1-craft), unit 10 (roles using art, design, tech or people skills, ma-g2-craft); every screening names roles as review |
| revision-log | New in kindergarten (ma-k-make, model_out) | Unit 3: the before-and-after card (the first card and the changed card side by side) | Unit 7 (a change tried and used to finish, ma-g1-make), unit 11 (a change near the end and its result, ma-g2-make) |
| critique-protocol | New in kindergarten (ma-k-judge, model_out) | Unit 3: the critique card "I notice, I like, I would change", handed to the children and scored. Units 1 and 2 hold APPROACH's critique routine (describe, ask, suggest) teacher-led, which is the same routine before the children own it | Unit 7 (the part that works best, a change for viewers, ma-g1-judge), unit 11 (how well it works where it is seen, ma-g2-judge); every critique as review |
| screening-plan | New in kindergarten (ma-k-present, model_out) | Unit 4: the screening-plan card in pictures (who does what, where it is shown) | Unit 8 (conditions and one task, ma-g1-present), unit 12 (conditions named, tasks carried out, ma-g2-present) |
| source-log | New in kindergarten (ma-k-sources, model_out) | Unit 4: "this came from me" on the strip's card (own experience or choice) | Unit 8 (an interest and a named example, ma-g1-sources), unit 12 (what I know, like and read, credited, ma-g2-sources) |

All eight go on to grade 3 (ma-g3 rows' model_in).


