188:## Seams
189:
190:### Picked up from the course before
191:
192:Kindergarten opens the band and the subject: there is no course before and no pre-kindergarten course. The eight
193:kindergarten threads that start here with no earlier row are ma-k-ideas, ma-k-make, ma-k-craft, ma-k-present,
194:ma-k-read, ma-k-judge, ma-k-society and ma-k-sources (their `assumes` cells are empty); each is first used in the unit
195:named in the table below.
196:
197:### Inside the band: year to year
198:
199:Each row of years 1 and 2 assumes the year before's row in its thread (one grade back), so it opens as a retrieval
200:task inside day 2 of its unit.
201:
202:| Thread | Year K row (unit, course days) | Year 1 row that picks it up (unit) | Year 2 row that picks it up (unit) | What changes |
203:|---|---|---|---|---|
204:| Reading media | ma-k-read (unit 1, days 1 to 18) | ma-g1-read (unit 5): retrieves noticing parts and messages, then names contents and compares how two pieces feel | ma-g2-read (unit 9) retrieves ma-g1-read (unit 5, days 65 to 82): describes how two pieces shape different experiences | Parts noticed, then contents named and two pieces compared, then how a piece shapes an experience described |
205:| Media in life and safe use | ma-k-society (unit 1, days 1 to 18) | ma-g1-society (unit 5): media links people you know; fair play and rules | ma-g2-society (unit 9) retrieves ma-g1-society (unit 5, days 65 to 82): media in cultural life, the idea of a media message | Media in my day and polite use, then links to people and fair rules, then culture and messages |
206:| Ideas and plans | ma-k-ideas (unit 2, days 19 to 40) | ma-g1-ideas (unit 6): three sketches in order and a mockup | ma-g2-ideas (unit 10) retrieves ma-g1-ideas (unit 6, days 83 to 104): many ideas, one chosen, a storyboard and mockup | Play and a first plan, then ideas in order, then many ideas and a choice |
207:| Tools and roles | ma-k-craft (unit 2, days 19 to 40) | ma-g1-craft (unit 6): named roles, a technique varied | ma-g2-craft (unit 10) retrieves ma-g1-craft (unit 6, days 83 to 104): roles with art, design, tech or people skills; named methods for recording and shaping | First hands on a tool, then named roles, then trying again and named methods |
208:| Making and changing | ma-k-make (unit 3, days 43 to 52) | ma-g1-make (unit 7): pattern and repetition, a change used to finish | ma-g2-make (unit 11) retrieves ma-g1-make (unit 7, days 107 to 116): several contents combined and placed to draw the eye | One change made on purpose, then a pattern named, then a whole placed for attention |
209:| Judging media | ma-k-judge (unit 3, days 43 to 52) | ma-g1-judge (unit 7): meaning, the part that works best, a change for viewers | ma-g2-judge (unit 11) retrieves ma-g1-judge (unit 7, days 107 to 116): purpose and setting, how well it works | Noticing and liking, then meaning and viewers, then purpose, setting and improvement |
210:| Joining and showing | ma-k-present (unit 4, days 55 to 64) | ma-g1-present (unit 8): a picture-book tale, one task in the showing | ma-g2-present (unit 12) retrieves ma-g1-present (unit 8, days 119 to 128): a narrated piece, the showing conditions named | Two art forms joined with help, then subject, art and sound in a tale, then one unified narrated piece |
211:| Sources and experience | ma-k-sources (unit 4, days 55 to 64) | ma-g1-sources (unit 8): an interest and a named example as sources | ma-g2-sources (unit 12) retrieves ma-g1-sources (unit 8, days 119 to 128): what you know, like and have read, credited | Own experience, then an example named, then reading and open sources credited |
212:
213:### Handed on to Media Arts, grades 3 to 5
214:
215:| This course hands on | Unit here | Row that picks it up (grade 3) | What grade 3 does with it |
216:|---|---|---|---|
217:| ma-g2-read | 9 | ma-g3-read | Takes apart how a piece's parts build its message and how a technique or style steers the audience |
218:| ma-g2-society | 9 | ma-g3-society | Media as a shaper of values and online behavior, tools and spaces examined for safe, fair use |
219:| ma-g2-ideas | 10 | ma-g3-ideas | Several ideas with different tools, tested with classmates before making |
220:| ma-g2-craft | 10 | ma-g3-craft | Group roles such as composing or tool handling; tools used in their standard ways |
221:| ma-g2-make | 11 | ma-g3-make | Content put in a purposeful order; a stressed element analyzed |
222:| ma-g2-judge | 11 | ma-g3-judge | The first named criteria, with a judgment given with them |
223:| ma-g2-present | 12 | ma-g3-present | A role and steps for sharing a piece, and a suggested improvement |
224:| ma-g2-sources | 12 | ma-g3-sources | An outside source and a source log; how popular media shapes meaning |
225:
