d media coordinated; MA:Pr6.1.4a, the kept screening-plan card (conditions explained, the role's steps), scored with a look-for on the role carried out; MA:Pr6.1.4b, a talk item: how the showing went and one improvement; MA:Cn10.1.4a, the kept source log: two sources credited and one line on what each informed; MA:Cn10.1.4b, a written item: one way an online space makes meaning or a shared experience, with the example. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: two formats compared (grade 5). Tools: the screening-plan card, the source log, the invented online space screens and role cards, Curio Class's own. Free path: drawn frames, a box stage, a printed showing program. Once-a-week path: 6 sessions | Last in year 4 because the public showing uses the year's stop-motion and crew (unit 6) and an arranged piece (unit 7), and ends the year after the year-end check (week 25); the screening plan and source log return from year 3 one step harder (a public showing, research) | Candidate: the school subject topics drawn from what the grade's science and social studies courses teach that term, listed on a topic card | Skawennati: the sensitivity agent reads the artist's own pages and a Kahnawà:ke community source first; no student imitates Kanien'kehá:ka designs or dress; CyberPowWow is studied by description and the still images on the artist's page, and no student goes online in class. Cultural knowledge is optional, with a public or invented topic marked the same, and no student is asked to explain their family's culture. Family yes for the public showing and any recording. Hazards and controls: a clear floor if a movement is joined; cords taped down; sound at a comfortable level. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
